---
import Flow from '../Flow.astro';
import WarpPipeline from './WarpPipeline.astro';
---
<figure class="figure">
  <div class="diagram">
    <Flow
      label="How a tile moves on H100"
      stages={[
        { title: 'Global memory (HBM)', items: ['Q, K, V tensors'] },
        { title: 'TMA', items: ['async bulk tile copy', 'no per-thread address math'] },
        { title: 'Shared memory', items: ['multi-stage tile buffer'] },
        { title: 'WGMMA', items: ['warpgroup MMA on tensor cores', 'operands read from shared memory'] },
      ]}
    />
  </div>
  <figcaption class="note">The Hopper data path that FlashAttention-3 is built around. Each of my kernels turned one of these features on or off.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure class="figure">
  <div class="diagram"><WarpPipeline /></div>
  <figcaption class="note">Warp specialization: while consumer warpgroups compute on one K/V tile, the producer warp is already loading the next. Illustrative, not to scale.</figcaption>
</figure>
